  <abstract format="text/plain" language="en" script="Latn">This Recommendation | International Standard, commonly knownas JBIG2, defines a coding method for bi-level images (e.g. black and whiteprinted matter). These are images consisting of a single rectangular bit plane,with each pixel taking on one of just two possible colours. This Recommendation| International Standard has been explicitly prepared for a lossy, lossless,and lossy-to-lossless image compression.</abstract>
